<h2>2. Problem Statement and Objectives</h2>

<h3>2.1 Problem Statement</h3>
Grassroots Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs) and civic bodies in India grapple with fragmented operations:
<li><strong>Siloed Coordination:</strong> Volunteer onboarding, scheduling, and attendance tracking are typically maintained across ad-hoc spreadsheets and messaging groups, causing high coordination friction and no verifiable service records.</li>
<li><strong>Philanthropic Opacity:</strong> Donors lack transparent, real-time insight into how their contributions impact targeted campaigns, and frequently face delays in receiving statutory Indian Income Tax Section 80G tax-deductible receipts.</li>
<li><strong>Administrative Workload:</strong> NGO staff are burdened with manual data entry, prone to service hour inflation, and struggle to provide accurate venue navigation for field volunteers.</li>

<h3>2.2 Objectives</h3>
The primary objective of the <strong>Community Care Portal</strong> is to engineer a consolidated, responsive, and secure platform that:
<ul><li>Enforces strict <strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</strong> across three isolated user personas: <strong>Volunteer</strong>, <strong>Donor</strong>, and <strong>Administrator</strong>.</li>
<li>Establishes a verified <strong>two-phase registration approval state machine</strong> (<code class="math-inline">\text{Pending} \rightarrow \text{Approved} \rightarrow \text{Attended}</code>) where administrators validate participants and log service hours directly into the volunteer's permanent audit ledger.</li>
<li>Embeds <strong>zero-API-key Google Maps deep-linking</strong> across localized community drives for native desktop and mobile smartphone navigation.</li>
<li>Provides <strong>instant 80G tax-deductible receipts</strong> with unique receipt identifiers (<code>#REC-2026-XXX</code>) alongside dynamic fundraising thermometers.</li>
<li>Equips NGO leadership with an <strong>administrative analytics dashboard</strong> featuring live registration filters and streaming CSV report exports.</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.3 Scope of the Project</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Functional Scope:</strong> Complete lifecycle management from landing discovery to registration review, financial checkout, and CSV audit downloads.</li>
<li><strong>Geographical Scope:</strong> Initial localized rollout tailored to prominent community hubs across <strong>Bengaluru and Karnataka</strong> (Majestic, HSR Layout, Ramanagara, Cubbon Park, Jayanagar, Koramangala, Hubballi, and Bannerghatta).</li>
<li><strong>Technical Scope:</strong> Decoupled Single Page Application (SPA) leveraging React 18, Vite 8, Node.js, Express, MongoDB, and dual-cloud continuous deployment on Vercel and Render.</li>
</ul>
<hr/>

<h2>3. Literature Survey and Research Gap</h2>

<h3>3.1 Review of Existing Platforms</h3>
<li><strong>VolunteerMatch / GivePulse (International):</strong> Comprehensive systems for matching volunteers to non-profits in Western regions. They lack rupee (<code class="math-inline">\text{₹}</code>) donation support, Indian Income Tax Section 80G compliance, and unified administrative beneficiary logs.</li>
<li><strong>Ketto / Milaap (Indian Crowdfunding):</strong> High-traffic medical and emergency crowdfunding portals. They focus exclusively on financial fundraising with no support for volunteer field events, shifts, or verified community hours.</li>
<li><strong>Manual Spreadsheets / Paper Records:</strong> The default tool for small Indian NGOs. Highly vulnerable to data loss, unauthorized edits, zero access security, and no automated notification mechanisms.</li>

<h3>3.2 Comparative Analysis Matrix</h3>

<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>Capability / Feature</th><th>VolunteerMatch</th><th>Ketto / Milaap</th><th>NGO Spreadsheets</th><th><strong>Community Care Portal (Our Work)</strong></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>Unified 3-in-1 Role Engine</strong></td><td>❌ (Volunteer only)</td><td>❌ (Donation only)</td><td>⚠️ (Disjointed files)</td><td>✅ <strong>Volunteer + Donor + Admin</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Two-Phase Registration Approval</strong></td><td>⚠️ Partial</td><td>❌ N/A</td><td>❌ Manual paper</td><td>✅ <strong>Automated State Machine</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Instant Digital 80G Tax Receipts</strong></td><td>❌ N/A</td><td>⚠️ Delayed email</td><td>❌ Manual receipt book</td><td>✅ <strong>Instant Automated Receipt</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Verified Service Hours Accounting</strong></td><td>❌ Self-reported</td><td>❌ N/A</td><td>❌ Prone to inflation</td><td>✅ <strong>Admin-Verified DB Ledger</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Zero-Cost Native Geolocation</strong></td><td>⚠️ Metered embed</td><td>❌ N/A</td><td>❌ Raw text string</td><td>✅ <strong>Universal Google Maps Intent</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Streaming Real-Time CSV Exports</strong></td><td>⚠️ Premium tier</td><td>⚠️ Summary only</td><td>⚠️ Manual save-as</td><td>✅ <strong>Built-in Streaming Export</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Regional Karnataka Localization</strong></td><td>❌ Global</td><td>⚠️ Pan-India</td><td>⚠️ Ad-hoc</td><td>✅ <strong>Curated Localized Hubs</strong></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>3.3 Identified Research Gaps</h3>
Existing software ecosystems force non-profits to operate separate tools for volunteer management and crowdfunding. There is a demonstrable gap for a <strong>zero-overhead, integrated solution</strong> that combines volunteer participation, transparent fundraising, verifiable service accounting, and localized regional navigation under a single access-controlled domain.

<hr/>

<h2>4. Data Description and Database Design</h2>

<h3>4.1 Schema Definitions & Data Entities</h3>
The application utilizes MongoDB with Mongoose object modeling:
<li><strong><code>User</code> Entity:</strong> Manages identity records, password digests (<code>bcryptjs</code>), role attributes (<code>Volunteer</code>, <code>Donor</code>, <code>Admin</code>), accumulated hours, and unlocked badges.</li>
<li><strong><code>Event</code> Entity:</strong> Stores scheduled drives, category tags, venue locations, capacity thresholds, attendee counts, and funding progress.</li>
<li><strong><code>Registration</code> Entity:</strong> Manages the relational connection between a Volunteer and an Event, tracking phone numbers, emergency contacts, notes, and approval status.</li>
<li><strong><code>Donation</code> Entity:</strong> Immutable financial ledger recording donor identity, campaign reference, rupee amount, and issued 80G tax receipt serials.</li>
<li><strong><code>Activity</code> Entity:</strong> Global audit timeline capturing platform events (registrations, donations, attendance confirmations).</li>
<li><strong><code>Beneficiary</code> Entity:</strong> Documents supported grassroots groups, assistance categories, and operational fulfillment statuses.</li>

<h3>4.2 Entity-Relationship (ER) Schema</h3>

<pre><code class="language-mermaid">erDiagram
    USER ||--o{ REGISTRATION : submits
    USER ||--o{ DONATION : contributes
    USER ||--o{ ACTIVITY : logs
    EVENT ||--o{ REGISTRATION : contains
    EVENT ||--o| CAMPAIGN : funds
    
    USER {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string name
        string email
        string password
        string role "Volunteer | Donor | Admin"
        number hoursLogged
        number eventsAttended
        string avatar
        date createdAt
    }

<p>EVENT {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string title
        string category "Community | Environment | Education | Healthcare"
        date date
        string location
        number spotsTotal
        ObjectId[] volunteersRegistered
        string status "Published | Upcoming | Completed"
        string image
        number campaignGoal
        number campaignRaised
    }</p>

<p>REGISTRATION {
        ObjectId _id PK
        ObjectId volunteerId FK
        string volunteerName
        string volunteerEmail
        string volunteerPhone
        ObjectId eventId FK
        string eventTitle
        string emergencyContact
        string notes
        string status "Pending | Approved | Attended | Rejected"
        number hoursLogged
        date createdAt
    }</p>

<p>DONATION {
        ObjectId _id PK
        ObjectId donorId FK
        string donorName
        string campaignTitle
        number amount
        string receiptId
        date createdAt
    }</p>

<p>ACTIVITY {
        ObjectId _id PK
        string title
        string type
        string user
        date createdAt
    }
</code></pre></p>

<h3>4.3 Central Shared Data Architecture (<code>portalData.js</code>)</h3>
To maintain consistency between volunteer registration cards, fundraising meters, and administrative queues, all 8 community initiatives are unified in <code>client/src/data/portalData.js</code>:
<ul><li><strong><code>SHARED_EVENTS</code></strong>: Master array of events with exact dates, locations, categories, capacity limits, and descriptions.</li>
<li><strong><code>SHARED_CAMPAIGNS</code></strong>: Computed directly from <code>SHARED_EVENTS</code>, ensuring philanthropic goals mirror real-world community events.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.4 Regional Seed Data (Karnataka & Bengaluru Landmarks)</h3>
All venues correspond to prominent Karnataka landmarks:
<li><strong>Food Drive at Majestic Center:</strong> <em>Majestic City Center, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Agara Lake Eco Cleanup Campaign:</strong> <em>Agara Lake, HSR Layout, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Rural School Supplies & Book Drive:</strong> <em>Govt Model Primary School, Ramanagara, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Cubbon Park & Nandi Hills Plantation:</strong> <em>Cubbon Park, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Senior Citizens Healthcare & Eye Camp:</strong> <em>Jayanagar 4th Block Community Hall, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Youth Digital Skills & Coding Workshop:</strong> <em>Koramangala Community Tech Hub, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Winter Blanket & Relief Distribution:</strong> <em>Hubballi Railway Station Relief Center, Hubballi, Karnataka</em></li>
<li><strong>Animal Welfare & Rescue Shelter Drive:</strong> <em>Bannerghatta Animal Care Sanctuary, Bengaluru, Karnataka</em></li>

