<h2>5. Methodology and System Architecture</h2>

<h3>5.1 System Architecture Diagram</h3>

<pre><code class="language-mermaid">flowchart TD
    User([Public User]) --&gt; Landing[Landing Page with Role Switcher]
    Landing --&gt; AuthCheck{Credentials & Role}
    
    AuthCheck --&gt;|Role: Volunteer| VolView[Volunteer Portal CarePortal.jsx]
    AuthCheck --&gt;|Role: Donor| DonView[Donor Dashboard DonorDashboard.jsx]
    AuthCheck --&gt;|Role: Admin| AdmView[Admin Dashboard AdminDashboard.jsx]
    
    subgraph Client Architecture
        VolView
        DonView
        AdmView
        DataLayer[(portalData.js)]
    end

<p>subgraph Backend REST Services
        NodeServer[Express Server on Render]
        AuthSvc[Auth & Role Guard]
        RegSvc[Registration & Approval Svc]
        DonSvc[Donation & 80G Svc]
        CSVSvc[CSV Streaming Engine]
    end</p>

<p>subgraph Persistence Layer
        DB[(MongoDB 7.0 / Atlas Cluster)]
    end</p>

<p>Client Architecture --&gt;|RESTful JSON / Bearer JWT| NodeServer
    NodeServer --&gt; AuthSvc & RegSvc & DonSvc & CSVSvc
    AuthSvc & RegSvc & DonSvc & CSVSvc --&gt; DB
    Client Architecture --&gt;|Zero-API Intent| Maps[Google Maps Mobile / Web]
</code></pre></p>

<h3>5.2 Registration Approval State Machine</h3>

<pre><code class="language-mermaid">stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --&gt; Pending : Volunteer Submits Registration Form
    note right of Pending : Form captured with phone & notes\nStatus: Acceptance: Pending\nVisible in Admin "Pending Approvals"
    
    Pending --&gt; Approved : Admin clicks "✓ Accept"
    note right of Approved : Notification dispatched to volunteer\nEvent card reflects "✓ Accepted"
    
    Pending --&gt; Rejected : Admin clicks "✕ Reject"
    note right of Rejected : Spot returned to event availability
    
    Approved --&gt; Attended : Admin marks attendance & inputs hours
    note right of Attended : Volunteer chart increments\nActivity recorded in MongoDB
    
    Attended --&gt; [*]
    Rejected --&gt; [*]
</code></pre>

<hr/>

<h2>6. Implementation Details</h2>

<h3>6.1 Technology Stack Summary</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Client Framework:</strong> React 18, Vite 8, React Router DOM 6</li>
<li><strong>Styling & Icons:</strong> CSS3 Design Tokens, Responsive Flexbox/Grid, Handcrafted Scalable SVG Icons</li>
<li><strong>Server Framework:</strong> Node.js v20, Express 4.x</li>
<li><strong>Database & ODM:</strong> MongoDB 7.0, Mongoose 8.x</li>
<li><strong>Security & Auth:</strong> JSON Web Tokens (JWT), bcryptjs password salting (10 rounds)</li>
<li><strong>Cloud Hosting:</strong> Vercel (Client SPA), Render (Containerized REST API)</li>
</ul>
<h3>6.2 Key Technical Innovations & Highlights</h3>

<p>#### 1. Zero-API-Key Google Maps Deep-Linking
Avoids heavy, billable Google Maps JavaScript SDKs by constructing RFC-compliant search intent URLs:
<pre><code class="language-javascript"><code>https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=${encodeURIComponent(event.location)}</code>
</code></pre>
<ul><li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Opens a new tab directly focused on the exact landmark.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Automatically launches the native Google Maps app with GPS turn-by-turn navigation.</li>
</ul>
#### 2. Browser History & Back-Button Guard
Prevents the common SPA defect where clicking the browser back button logs the user out:
<pre><code class="language-javascript">useEffect(() =&gt; {
  window.history.pushState({ tab: 'dashboard' }, '');
  const handlePopState = () =&gt; {
    if (modalRef.current) {
      setModal(null);
      window.history.pushState({ tab: tabRef.current }, '');
      return;
    }
    if (tabRef.current !== 'dashboard') {
      setTab('dashboard');
      window.history.pushState({ tab: 'dashboard' }, '');
    } else {
      window.history.pushState({ tab: 'dashboard' }, '');
    }
  };
  window.addEventListener('popstate', handlePopState);
  return () =&gt; window.removeEventListener('popstate', handlePopState);
}, []);
</code></pre></p>

<p>#### 3. Viewport-Locked Full-Height Layout Architecture
<ul><li>Outer container styled with <code>height: 100vh; maxHeight: 100vh; overflow: hidden</code>.</li>
<li>Sidebar styled with <code>height: 100vh; minWidth: 200px; background: #0a3d24</code>, extending 100% to the bottom of the page with zero white gap.</li>
<li>Independent main container scrolling (<code>overflowY: auto; overflowX: hidden</code>).</li>
</ul>
#### 4. Instant 80G Tax-Deductible Donation Engine
<ul><li>Instant calculation and receipt generation with unique receipt codes (e.g., <code>#REC-2026-881</code>).</li>
<li>Donor receipt history table with download actions.</li>
</ul>
#### 5. Privilege Escalation Defense
<ul><li>In <code>authController.js</code>, public signup payloads with <code>role: 'admin'</code> are automatically forced to <code>role: 'volunteer'</code>, locking administrative access to pre-provisioned credentials.</li>
</ul>
<hr/></p>

