<h2>9. Limitations</h2>
<li><strong>Payment Gateway Mocking:</strong> Financial donations currently trigger authenticated sandbox checkouts and generate 80G receipts directly, but require commercial Razorpay or Stripe merchant accounts for live bank card authorization.</li>
<li><strong>Push Notifications:</strong> Notification updates currently rely on browser-level storage and WebSocket/polling mechanisms; Native Web Push API notifications for background mobile alerts can be added in future versions.</li>
<li><strong>Automated Geofencing:</strong> Attendance verification is currently confirmed by an authorized administrator rather than automated GPS geofencing radius checks on volunteer smartphones.</li>

<hr/>

<h2>10. Conclusion and Future Scope</h2>

<h3>10.1 Conclusion</h3>
The <strong>Community Care Portal</strong> successfully addresses the fragmentation, lack of transparency, and operational friction prevalent in non-profit operations. By bridging <strong>Volunteers</strong>, <strong>Donors</strong>, and <strong>Administrators</strong> under a responsive, role-guarded React/Node ecosystem, the platform demonstrates how modern web engineering can elevate community welfare. From deep-linked navigation for grassroots Karnataka drives to two-phase registration state machines and instant 80G tax receipting, the project delivers a complete, production-grade solution.

<h3>10.2 Future Scope</h3>
<li><strong>Live Payment Gateway Integration:</strong> Connecting live Razorpay/UPI APIs to enable instantaneous INR settlements.</li>
<li><strong>QR-Code Volunteer Passports:</strong> Generating unique mobile QR codes for volunteers that event coordinators can scan on-site for automated zero-touch attendance logging.</li>
<li><strong>Multilingual Regional Support:</strong> Integrating Kannada language localization (<code>kn-IN</code>) to broaden grassroots accessibility across rural Karnataka gram panchayats.</li>
<li><strong>PWA (Progressive Web App) Packaging:</strong> Adding service workers to allow offline event schedules and native mobile homescreen installations.</li>

